rtainly  could be done this could be attached to  a real-time display just as easily so  you're in a sense watching something  that looks very much like a like a  weather you know weather report from  weather bug or something like that  you're watching what's actually  happening instead of a simulated  forecast of what's going on all right so  that's that was one assignment that was  a lot of fun to put together and we were  we were kind of amazed at how quickly we  could put together we built the scene in  about three or four days our studio  built the scene about three or four days  and then we put the interface together  in another sort of week or so so unity  made it easy for us to do this so the  integration wasn't as difficult as we  thought it would be and I think that's  really good news all right the second  the second application that we had was  one of oil and gas drilling a nother oil  company came to us oilfield services  company came to us actually and we're  asking us about this whole  unconventional drilling now you've  probably heard all the press about  fracking hydraulic fracture fracturing  underneath to to drive the oil and gas  particles in the way that you want to  drive them kind of controversial  actually but in essence the  energy industry is really a bit  flummoxed about this whole idea of  unconventional drilling conventional  drilling is you stick up a pipe in a  hole and out comes the oil  unconventional drilling is much more  like mining it's kind of like mining  underground you're you're crushing rock  underground it's very the technologies  are different the geology is different  it's different in every kind of way so  they wanted to really understand  basically how does this viscous fluid  oil and gas and mud and water all mixed  together sort of moving through cracks  in rock so that's when we had a chance  to work with what I think is is a really  powerful part of unity which is the  particle system and I think it probably  lots of applications of the particle  system essentially it allows you to take  some medium that is particulate in  nature so fire or smoke or some kind of  liquid or fog or clouds and and  represent it in a real physics kind of  way inside of unity it's a very kind of  sophisticated and complicated system to  work with but it allows you a whole lot  of flexibility so the challenge for us  was figuring out if in fact we could we  could do this so we created for  ourselves a stimulation source that's  the that blue pipe so imagine that's the  the thing that's injecting this fluid in  there breaking up rocks and then we  created for ourselves an extraction  source so this is pipe that's gonna suck  up the stuff that comes its way so when  we do that we can see that there's the  the gas and oil mixture believe that gas  is the purple and the the oil mixture is  green and still early days and this  we're still playing around with this but  essentially that's the way the stuff is  moving through these rocks we've cut the  rocks away and made them invisible and  we're imagining this fluid sort of  winding its way through this kind of  these capillaries ultim  headed toward the extraction source so  it could be sucked up and they're  testing all kinds of technologies for  making this work and what they wanted to  use was the combination of Mathematica  to do the calculations and then unity to  show how it actually worked so in other  words Mathematica is doing the the  capillary flow calculations we used this  thing called lattice Boltzmann equations  to say alright this piece of fluid is  going to move this way and this piece of  fluid is going to move that way and  wrote up all those calculations  generated another one of these script  files like I was showing you earlier and  it in turn makes the the fluid flow  because the the particle system in unity  is so flexible it allowed us to kind of  program it if you will  to make it move in the way we needed it  to move in color i